.
"are you angry"
( prob { ?_you /pres emotion [k anger ] } )
.
"are you angry with $person(Q_NP)"
( prob { ?_you /pres emotion [k anger ] $person(Q_NP) } )
.
"are you grieving"
( prob { ?_you /pres emotion [k grief ] } )
.
"do you grieve for $person(Q_NP)"
( prob { ?_you /pres emotion [k grief ] $person(Q_NP) } )
.
"do you feel guilty"
( prob { ?_you /pres emotion [k guilt ] } )
.

# # FLAG: "why are you upset / why were you angry / why did you fear him" needs
# WH-why parsing (discourse_planner: why-questions are unsupported) normalised
# onto a cause predicate. Truly-new work; the cause chain exists (/caused_by).


# --- 10. ALIBI (extends the crime-night set already above) -------------------

"where were you on the night of the murder"
( whereabouts_on ?_you ( night_of ( death_date $person(Q_NP) ) ) ).target
.
"can you account for your whereabouts the night $person(Q_NP) died"
( whereabouts_on ?_you ( night_of ( death_date $person(Q_NP) ) ) ).target
.
"where were you the morning $person(Q_NP) was killed"
( whereabouts_on ?_you ( morning_of ( death_date $person(Q_NP) ) ) ).target
.

# # FLAG: an inspector-named clock time ("where were you at nine") needs a
# band-from-clock-time func; only crime-anchored day-bands resolve today.


# =============================================================================
# OBJECT-CENTRIC FORMS  (+ inline-alternation demonstration)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# People ask about the SPECIFIC entity behind a fact - "what church do you
# attend", "what firm employs you", "who is your closest friend" - not just the
# abstract category. These forms return the bound object (a building / org /
# person) via ( any { ... } ).target or ( o /known { ... @o } ).
#
# They also exercise the new inline-alternation syntax: "[go to|attend]" in a
# phrase literal expands at LOAD time to one row per branch, all sharing this
# meaning. Brackets are used (not parens) so the delimiter never collides with
# a $hole(...) or a kind literal [k ...]. Branches may be multi-word and may
# contain holes. REQUIRES the rebuilt parser (t_nat_lang::_expand_nl_
# alternations); until then these lines read as literal text and will not match.
# Each `[a|b]` below replaces what would otherwise be 2-4 near-duplicate lines.
# =============================================================================

# --- Residence / birthplace (object) -----------------------------------------
"[what|which] [house|address] do you [live at|reside at]"
( any { ?_you /pres home } ).target
.
"[what|which] [town|parish] were you born in"
( any { ?_you /pres birthplace } ).target
.

# --- Profession: the employer ENTITY (org) -----------------------------------
"[what|which] [firm|house|establishment|concern] [do you work for|employs you]"
( o /known { ?_you /pres employer @o } )
.
"[who|what house] does $person(Q_NP) [work for|serve]"
( o /known { $person(Q_NP) /pres employer @o } )
.

# --- Routine: the church / public-house ENTITY (building) --------------------
"[what|which] [church|chapel] do you [attend|worship at|go to]"
( any { ?_you /pres worship ? } ).target
.
"[what|which] [public house|tavern|inn] do you [drink at|frequent]"
( any { ?_you /pres indulge ? } ).target
.

# --- Social: the specific person -------------------------------------------
"who is your [closest|dearest|best] friend"
( o /known { ?_you /pres friend @o } )
.
"who do you [trust most|rely on]"
( o /known { ?_you /pres trust @o } )
.

# --- Romance: the specific person -------------------------------------------
"who are you [courting|sweet on|fond of]"
( o /known { ?_you /pres fancy @o } )
.

# --- Criminal: the suspected person -----------------------------------------
"who do you [suspect|think did it|believe is guilty]"
( o /known { ?_you /pres suspect @o } )
.

# --- Education: the school ENTITY (object) -----------------------------------
# # FLAG: the school as an ENTITY is NOT in the substrate - hsim mints
# {pupil study <curriculum>} with the SUBJECT as target and leaves study's
# (aux org) institution slot unset (hse_engine.cc enroll), and there is no
# `.aux` accessor. So this returns @unknown today. To answer it: (1) hsim must
# set study's aux org to the school entity at enroll, and (2) add a `.aux`
# post-eval field accessor (parallel to `.target`/`.label`/`.sub`). The phrasing
# is staged here so it is ready the moment the substrate lands; for now it
# best-effort confirms WHAT was studied, not WHERE.
"[what|which] school did you [go to|attend|study at]"
( any { ?_you /ever study ? } ).target
.
